+# [MP8] ═══ Which device to throw when throw is pressed (bug reported by the user from real gameplay on 2026-08-25) ═══
+#
+# **This used to go through `_mp8_dev()`**, which **falls back to the device from setup** when `mp8_current_device` is empty —
+# and that device may well be riding on **someone else's** back, or already flying through the air.
+#
+# Measured in the host's 8-24 match (`godot.log`, 6 players). Throw was pressed **159** times across the match, and **61** of those landed on
+# an unbound device. deamn alone pressed throw 76 times, 58 of them empty throws (**76%**),
+# along with **51 `Device: Transition From Thrown to Thrown`** self-transitions —
+# which means a device that was **already in flight** kept getting thrown again.
+#
+# ### Why "the press goes through but the server has no binding" happens
+#
+# `has_spine_breaker` (the **client's** throw gate, the first line of `update_throwing()`) and
+# `mp8_current_device` (the binding the **server** records) are **two separate pieces of state**,
+# maintained by two **different RPCs**, `set_spine_breaker_rpc()` and `mp8_bind_rpc()`.
+# If the two get out of step by even one beat (or the bind is overwritten by a device that stuck later),
+# the client can press throw while the server side is empty.
+#
+# ### The fix — ask the device itself, don't guess
+#
+# `attached_to` is the authoritative fact (who it's riding on) written by `attached_state` on the **server**.
+#   1. Trust `mp8_current_device` first, but it **only** counts if `attached_to == self`.
+#   2. If that doesn't match, scan the devices on the field for the one with `attached_to == self`.
+#   3. If neither finds one = there's truly nothing on the back → **don't throw**.
+#
+# This also fixes those 51 self-transitions. A device already in flight has `attached_to` as null, so the scan won't find it and it naturally won't be re-thrown.
+#
+# ⚠️ **Only call this on the server**. On clients `attached_to` is always null
+#    (the device state machine only runs on the server, see that comment in `spine_breaker_device.gd`).
+# ⚠️ The fallback in `_mp8_dev()` **is left untouched** — the death reset path (`break_spine`) still uses it,
+#    and there falling back to the setup device means "better to move the wrong one than not move one at all", the opposite trade-off from here.
+func _mp8_dev_to_throw() -> SpineBreakerDevice :
+
+	if mp8_current_device != null and is_instance_valid(mp8_current_device) \
+			and mp8_current_device.attached_to == self:
+		return mp8_current_device
+
+	if game_instance != null:
+		var list = game_instance.get("_mp8_devices")
+		if list is Array:
+			for d in list:
+				if is_instance_valid(d) and d.attached_to == self:
+					return d
+
+	return null
+
